All 15 tests pass (`15 passed in 0.02s`), no skip/xfail markers anywhere, and nothing under `tests/` was touched.

Fixes, per module:

**`src/auth.py`**
- `has_permission` now matches roles case-insensitively (`role.lower() == required.lower()`), so `["Admin"]` grants `"admin"` — `src/auth.py:10`.
- `is_admin_or_owner` used `and`; changed to `or` so admin alone or owner alone grants access — `src/auth.py:15`.

**`src/inventory.py`**
- Mutable default `initial={}` caused shared state between instances; now `None` → fresh dict, and the caller's dict is copied — `src/inventory.py:13`.
- `add` overwrote stock; now accumulates — `src/inventory.py:20`.
- `reserve` used `qty >= available` (blocking full-reserve); changed to `>`, so reserving exactly the available amount is allowed — `src/inventory.py:28`.
- `release` allowed negative reserved counts; now raises `ValueError` when releasing more than reserved — `src/inventory.py:35-36`.

**`src/text_utils.py`**
- `slugify` now lowercases and collapses repeated separators to completion (single `replace("--","-")` only merged pairs, leaving `hello--world`) — `src/text_utils.py:18-23`.
- `truncate` didn't account for suffix length; now slices to `max_len - len(suffix)` so the total including `…` stays within `max_len` — `src/text_utils.py:33`.
